 "post": {
  "instagram": "A gap fill means price trades back to yesterday's close. One way to trade it: wait for the first 15 minutes, enter on a close below their low, stop above the day's high, target yesterday's close. Example: a 1.1% gap, entry 100.96, stop 101.73, target 100.00. Big news gaps often don't fill, so you need the failure first.\n\nSave this for later and follow @calmedgeofficial for one trading concept a day.\n\nEducational example on an illustrative chart. Not financial advice; trading involves risk of loss.\n\n#gapfill #daytradingstrategy #gaptrading #tradingeducation #technicalanalysis #daytrading #trading #learntotrade",
